45
00:03:58,359 --> 00:04:02,040
You're crazy," mumbled Zuckerman.

46
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:04,840
But she paid no attention to him.

47
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:07,478
Together, they walked to the pig pin.

48
00:04:07,478 --> 00:04:14,680
Mrs. Zuckerman wasted no time. She climbed in with Wilbur and went to work.

49
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:19,639
Dipping her paddle in the buttermilk, she rubbed him all over. The geese

50
00:04:19,639 --> 00:04:24,920
gathered around to see the fun, and so did the sheep and lambs. Even Templeton

51
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:31,159
poked his head out cautiously to watch Wilbur get a buttermilk bath. Charlotte

52
00:04:31,159 --> 00:04:36,279
got so interested she lowered herself on a drag line so she could see better.

53
00:04:36,279 --> 00:04:40,279
Wilbur stood still and closed his eyes.

54
00:04:40,279 --> 00:04:45,959
He could feel the buttermilk trickling down his sides.

55
00:04:45,959 --> 00:04:51,639
He opened his mouth and some buttermilk ran in. It was delicious.

56
00:04:51,639 --> 00:04:55,000
He felt radiant and happy when Mrs.

57
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:03,559
Zuckermanman got through and rubbed him dry. He was the cleanest, prettiest pig you ever saw.

58
00:05:03,559 --> 00:05:10,680
He was pure white, pink around the ears and snout, and smooth as silk. The

59
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:15,639
Zuckermanman's went up to change into their best clothes. Lurvy went to shave

60
00:05:15,639 --> 00:05:21,000
and put on his plaid shirt and his purple necktie. The animals were left to

61
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,120
themselves in the barn.

62
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:29,398
The seven gosslings paraded round and round their mother. "Please, please,

63
00:05:29,398 --> 00:05:34,920
please take us to the fair," begged a gozling. Then all seven began teasing to

64
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:43,799
go. "Please, please, please, please." They made quite a racket. Children,

65
00:05:43,799 --> 00:05:50,600
snapped the goose. We're staying quietly idly, idly at home. Only Wilbury Il is

66
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:53,478
going to the fair.

67
00:05:53,478 --> 00:06:00,600
Just then, Charlotte interrupted. I shall go too, she said softly. I have

68
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:08,359
decided to go with Wilbur. He may need me. We can't tell what may happen at the fairgrounds.

69
00:06:08,359 --> 00:06:13,079
Somebody's got to go along who knows how to write, and I think Templeton better

70
00:06:13,079 --> 00:06:19,959
come, too. I might need somebody to run errands and do general work.

71
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:27,478
I'm staying right here, grumbled the rat. I haven't the slightest interest in

72
00:06:27,478 --> 00:06:35,639
fairs. That's because you've never been to one, remarked the old sheep. A fair

73
00:06:35,639 --> 00:06:38,680
is a rat's paradise.

74
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:45,559
Everybody spills food at a fair. A rat can creep out late at night and have a

75
00:06:45,559 --> 00:06:54,040
feast. In the horse barn, you will find oats that the trotters and paces have spilled.

76
00:06:54,040 --> 00:07:00,359
In the trampled grass of the infield, you will find old discarded lunchboxes

77
00:07:00,359 --> 00:07:06,359
containing the foul remains of peanut butter sandwiches, hardboiled eggs,

78
00:07:06,359 --> 00:07:13,719
cracker crumbs, bits of donuts, and particles of cheese.

79
00:07:13,719 --> 00:07:18,600
In the hard pack dirt of the midway, after the glaring lights are out and the

80
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:25,398
people have gone home to bed, you will find a veritable treasure of popcorn

81
00:07:25,398 --> 00:07:31,959
fragments, frozen custard ribblings, candid apples abandoned by tired

82
00:07:31,959 --> 00:07:39,318
children, sugar fluff crystals, salted almonds, popsicles, partially gnawed ice

83
00:07:39,318 --> 00:07:50,120
cream cones, and the wooden sticks of lollipops. S everywhere is loot for a rat in tents

84
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:56,439
and booths and hoffs. Why a fair has enough disgusting leftover food to

85
00:07:56,439 --> 00:08:00,040
satisfy a whole army of rats.

86
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:09,239
Templeton's eyes were blazing. "Is this true?" he asked. "Is this uh appetizing

87
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:18,040
ya yours true? I like high living and what you say pimps me.

88
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:26,040
It is true, said the old sheep. Go to the fair, Templeton. You will find that

89
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:32,920
the conditions at a fair will surpass your wildest dreams.

90
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:36,279
Buckets with sour mash sticking to them.

91
00:08:36,279 --> 00:08:42,840
Tin cans containing particles of tuna fish. Reeseasy paper bag stuffed with

92
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:45,719
rotten "That's enough," cried Templeton.

93
00:08:45,719 --> 00:08:49,000
"Don't tell me anymore. I'm going."

94
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:54,920
"Good," said Charlotte, winking at the old sheep.

95
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:58,439
"Now then, there is no time to be lost.

96
00:08:58,439 --> 00:09:01,079
Wilbur will soon be put into the crate.

97
00:09:01,079 --> 00:09:06,520
Templeton and I must get in the crate right now and hide ourselves." The rat

98
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:11,799
didn't waste a minute. He scampered over to the crate, crawled between the slats,

99
00:09:11,799 --> 00:09:17,079
and pulled straw up over him so he was hidden from sight.

100
00:09:17,079 --> 00:09:20,920
"All right," said Charlotte. "I'm next."

101
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:27,559
She sailed into the air, let out a drag line, and dropped gently to the ground.

102
00:09:27,559 --> 00:09:32,359
Then she climbed the side of the crate, and hid herself inside a knot hole in

103
00:09:32,359 --> 00:09:36,520
the top board. The old sheep nodded.

104
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:49,040
What a cargo. She said that sign ought to say Zuckerman's famous pig and two stowways.

105
00:09:49,079 --> 00:09:50,920
Look out.

106
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:53,478
The people are coming.

107
00:09:53,478 --> 00:09:58,760
Shouted the gander. Cheese it, cheese it, cheese it. The big truck with Mr.

108
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:03,959
Rarable at the wheel back slowly down toward the barnyard. Lurvy and Mr.

109
00:10:03,959 --> 00:10:08,439
Zuckerman walked alongside. Fern and Avery were standing in the body of the

110
00:10:08,439 --> 00:10:11,879
truck, hanging on to the sideboards.

111
00:10:11,879 --> 00:10:17,959
"Listen to me," whispered the old sheep to Wilbur. "When they open the crate and

112
00:10:17,959 --> 00:10:25,159
try to put you in, struggle. Don't go without a tussle. Pigs always resist

113
00:10:25,159 --> 00:10:32,040
when they are being loaded." "If I struggle, I'll get dirty," said Wilbur.

114
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:36,840
Never mind that. Do as I say, struggle.

115
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:41,000
If you were to walk into the crate without resisting, Zuckerman might think

116
